module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_imported_name_shadowed_by_a_kernel_name

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data an_imported_name_shadowed_by_a_kernel_name: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_imported_name_shadowed_by_a_kernel_name" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "an imported name shadowed by a kernel name: a module writes `import m { Optional }`, naming a declaration m owns, and the v1 resolver binds every bare `Optional` in that module to the KERNEL Optional instead. The kernel scope layer sits positionally above direct imports (v1.compiler.infer direct_import_export_precedence_note: locals > kernel > direct-selected > transitive), and v1.compiler.infer_env overlay_skips_kernel_name lists the names no import overrides: every kernel type, the container names, Unit, Optional, Present and Absent. INVALID STATE: an authored import that selects a declaration and has no effect on what the name denotes. Nothing refuses.",

    "HARM: silent wrongness (DESIGN section 5). The author named a declaration and the program is typed, emitted and run against a different one. Where the imported declaration's shape differs from the kernel's, the module's values stop inhabiting the type the author wrote, and every verdict over them is the kernel's.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the name is one overlay_skips_kernel_name admits; the module imports it BY NAME from a module that declares it; the module does not itself declare it. A module's OWN declaration of the leaf does shadow the kernel (locals sit above the kernel layer), so the same spelling declared locally is not this class. FOUND 2026-10-06 on gunbc#13454 (native broker 2K-b): the side-chat review asked the emitter to realize such an imported Optional as the imported coproduct, which would have forked the emitter's answer from the resolver's (DESIGN section 3, operator ruling via gentle-dove-36). The emitter instead follows the resolver's order through v1.compiler.infer_env bare_occurrence_binding, and the class is filed here, at the resolver, which owns it.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor -- silent, unrefused, and pinned today by gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls_optional_importer, a module importing gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls_optional_collision Optional whose bare uses resolve and realize as the kernel Optional (cases optional_imported_name_binds_the_kernel_option_*). The v2 resolver already refuses the Int instance of this class (v2.compiler.resolve resolve_atom; v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation bla_imported_user_int_refuses_rather_than_binding_the_kernel_int). ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- the collision is decidable at the import, from the import's selected declaration and the kernel name set. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain: the v1 resolver REFUSES, at the import, every named import of a name overlay_skips_kernel_name admits when the selected declaration is not the one the kernel name denotes, over every such name and not only Optional. When it lands the importer fixture stops compiling, and the controls pinning today's answer are rewritten as the refusal's discriminating red.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "direct_import_export_precedence_note", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_env", decl_name: "overlay_skips_kernel_name", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_env", decl_name: "bare_occurrence_binding", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls_optional_importer", decl_name: "HeldChoice", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation", decl_name: "bla_imported_user_int_refuses_rather_than_binding_the_kernel_int", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
